# Firebase Crash Hunter — Configuration
# Copy this file to .crash-hunter in your repo root (it's gitignored)
# All values can also be set as environment variables instead.

# ── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Google Cloud / Firebase project ID
# Find it: cat android/google-services.json | grep project_id
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=my-firebase-project

# Your Android app's package name (from build.gradle / app.id)
ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME=com.example.myapp

# ── Optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# BigQuery dataset name (default: firebase_crashlytics)
# BQ_DATASET=firebase_crashlytics

# Override the table name if yours differs from the default
# Default is derived as: ${ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME//./_}_ANDROID
# BQ_TABLE=com_example_myapp_ANDROID

# Path to your repo root (default: current working directory)
# REPO_ROOT=/path/to/your/repo

# Path to your CLAUDE.md rules file (default: $REPO_ROOT/CLAUDE.md)
# If not found, universal Kotlin/Android rules are used automatically.
# CLAUDE_MD_PATH=/path/to/CLAUDE.md

# Override the claude binary path (default: auto-detected from PATH)
# CLAUDE_BIN=/home/user/.nvm/versions/node/v20/bin/claude

# Log file location (default: same directory as crash_hunter.sh)
# LOG_FILE=/tmp/crash_hunter.log
